(Question: What is the RIA 2022 minimum investment threshold for TEA projects?) Tj
0 -20 Td
(Answer: Under the EB-5 Reform and Integrity Act of 2022 (RIA), the minimum qualifying investment in a Targeted Employment Area (TEA) is $800,000.) Tj
0 -35 Td
(Question: Can H-1B or L-1 visa holders file concurrently under EB-5?) Tj
0 -20 Td
(Answer: Yes! Concurrent filing of Form I-526E and Form I-485 is permitted for lawful nonimmigrants currently in the United States, granting immediate travel and work authorization.) Tj
0 -35 Td
(Question: What is the required job creation rule under USCIS standards?) Tj
0 -20 Td
(Answer: Each qualifying investment must create or preserve at least 10 full-time jobs for qualifying U.S. workers for at least 2 years.) Tj
